libbpf: make next_path const in resolve_full_path()

glibc 2.43 (C23) makes strchr() return const char * for a const char *
argument. The libbpf bundled with rpi kernel 6.6.78 assigns that to a
plain char *, which trips -Wdiscarded-qualifiers and, under the tools
build's -Werror, breaks tools/bpf/resolve_btfids (and the whole kernel
build). Same change as upstream libbpf's C23 const fix.

--- a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
@@ -11233,7 +11233,7 @@
 		if (!search_paths[i])
 			continue;
 		for (s = search_paths[i]; s != NULL; s = strchr(s, ':')) {
-			char *next_path;
+			const char *next_path;
 			int seg_len;
 
 			if (s[0] == ':')
